+  # ⚠️ The V1 line is what makes a PCIe rig scoreable at all: SGLang admits V2
+  # only on a full NVLink mesh (can_use_custom_all_reduce_v2 -> full_nvlink), so
+  # every PCIe rig runs V1 and could otherwise never report better than
+  # `unknown` while its kernel was demonstrably live (#1462 follow-up).
+  # A veto still outranks this within one boot — the two are mutually exclusive
+  # in the engine, and if both ever appear the refusal is what we must not paper
+  # over. Hence: matched here, APPLIED after Step 2's verdicts.
+  engine_engaged=""
+  case "$text" in
+    *"All Reduce config:"*|*"cuda graph addresses"*) engine_engaged=yes ;;
+  esac
+
